{#def
    settings: DownloadClientSettings,
#}

<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h3 class="text-base">
        Download clients
    </h3>
    <p class="text-xs opacity-60">
        Optional, but much more reliable. Without one, a finished download is found by matching the
        release name against folder names, which fails when the client renames the folder. With one,
        Earr asks the client exactly where it put the files, and knows when a download is still
        running or has failed rather than guessing.
    </p>

    <form class="flex flex-col gap-2"
          hx-put="{{ base_url }}/settings/library/hx-download-clients"
          hx-disabled-elt="#dc-save">
        <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-t pt-3 border-base-200">
            <label for="qbit-enabled" class="font-semibold">
                qBittorrent <span class="text-xs font-normal opacity-60">(torrents)</span>
            </label>
            <input id="qbit-enabled"
                   name="qbit_enabled"
                   type="checkbox"
                   class="checkbox"
                   {% if settings.qbit_enabled %}checked{% endif %} />
        </div>
        <input name="qbit_url"
               type="text"
               value="{{ settings.qbit_url }}"
               placeholder="http://192.168.0.102:8080"
               class="input w-full" />
        <div class="flex gap-2">
            <input name="qbit_username"
                   type="text"
                   value="{{ settings.qbit_username }}"
                   placeholder="username (blank if the host is whitelisted)"
                   class="input w-full" />
            <input name="qbit_password"
                   type="password"
                   {% if settings.qbit_password_set %}placeholder="●●●●●●●● (unchanged)"{% else %}placeholder="password"{% endif %}
                   class="input w-full" />
        </div>

        <input name="qbit_category"
               type="text"
               value="{{ settings.qbit_category }}"
               placeholder="category to move grabs into, e.g. books (blank to leave alone)"
               class="input w-full" />

        <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-t pt-3 border-base-200">
            <label for="sab-enabled" class="font-semibold">
                SABnzbd <span class="text-xs font-normal opacity-60">(usenet)</span>
            </label>
            <input id="sab-enabled"
                   name="sab_enabled"
                   type="checkbox"
                   class="checkbox"
                   {% if settings.sab_enabled %}checked{% endif %} />
        </div>
        <input name="sab_url"
               type="text"
               value="{{ settings.sab_url }}"
               placeholder="http://192.168.0.103:8080"
               class="input w-full" />
        <input name="sab_api_key"
               type="password"
               {% if settings.sab_api_key_set %}placeholder="●●●●●●●● (unchanged)"{% else %}placeholder="API key"{% endif %}
               class="input w-full" />

        <input name="sab_category"
               type="text"
               value="{{ settings.sab_category }}"
               placeholder="category to move grabs into, e.g. books (blank to leave alone)"
               class="input w-full" />

        <p class="text-xs opacity-60 pt-1">
            Prowlarr picks the category when it hands a release to the client and offers no way to
            override it, so Earr moves the download afterwards. In qBittorrent this relocates the
            files if the category has a save path and Auto Torrent Management is on, which is usually
            the point. SABnzbd can only recategorise a job that is still in the queue.
        </p>

        <div class="flex gap-2 pt-2">
            <button id="dc-save" class="btn btn-primary">
                Save
            </button>
            <button type="button"
                    class="btn"
                    hx-post="{{ base_url }}/settings/library/hx-test-download-clients"
                    hx-disabled-elt="this">
                Test connection
            </button>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs opacity-60">
            Leave a password or API key blank to keep the stored one. Paths must look the same to Earr
            as they do to the client, which for Docker means mounting them the same way in both.
        </p>
    </form>
</div>
